# AGENTS.md

## Project overview

Single-page marketing / VIP-waitlist landing site for **xstinkt**, a patent-pending
odor-eliminating garbage-can system (Indiegogo early-bird launch). The site collects
emails and presents product info across stacked sections. Built and synced via
**Lovable.dev**.

## Tech stack

Vite 5 · React 18 · TypeScript 5 · shadcn-ui (Radix) · Tailwind CSS 3 · react-router-dom 6
· @tanstack/react-query 5 · react-hook-form + zod · @supabase/supabase-js 2 ·
framer-motion · lucide-react. Tests: Vitest + Testing Library + jsdom. Lint: ESLint 9
(flat config). Package manager: **npm**.

## Architecture map

- `src/main.tsx` → mounts the app.
- `src/App.tsx` → providers (QueryClient, Tooltip, Toasters) + router. Add new routes
  **above** the catch-all `*` route.
- `src/pages/Index.tsx` → composes the landing page sections in display order.
- `src/components/*.tsx` → one file per page section (Navigation, Hero, Problem,
  HowItWorks, Models, About, Contact, Footer).
- `src/components/ui/*` → shadcn-ui primitives (generated; treat as vendored).
- `src/hooks/`, `src/lib/utils.ts` (`cn()` helper).
- `src/integrations/supabase/` → Supabase client + generated types.

Path alias: `@` → `src/`.

## Setup

```sh
npm install        # or: npm ci
npm run dev        # Vite dev server on http://localhost:8080
```

## Commands (run before every commit)

```sh
npm run lint       # eslint .
npm run test       # vitest run
npm run build      # production build (catches most type/import errors)
```

There is **no** dedicated typecheck or format script. For a strict type pass use
`npx tsc --noEmit`.

## Coding conventions

- TypeScript + functional React components with hooks.
- Use the `@/...` import alias for everything under `src/`.
- Styling is **Tailwind utility classes**; compose conditional classes with `cn()` from
  `@/lib/utils`. Don't introduce CSS-in-JS or new styling systems.
- Reuse existing `src/components/ui/*` primitives instead of hand-rolling buttons,
  inputs, dialogs, etc.
- Keep each landing section self-contained in its own `src/components/*Section.tsx`
  file and register it in `src/pages/Index.tsx`.
- Match the existing file's naming, structure, and comment density.

## Dependency rules

- Prefer existing dependencies (see `package.json`) before adding new ones.
- Do **not** install new packages without being asked; call it out first.
- For new UI primitives, add the corresponding shadcn-ui component rather than a new
  unrelated library.

## Security rules

- **Never commit secrets.** Reference env vars by name only (`VITE_SUPABASE_URL`,
  `VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`, `VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID`).
- `.env` is currently git-tracked — do not add new secrets to it; flag this if asked to
  touch env config.
- Only `VITE_`-prefixed vars are exposed to the client by Vite — never put a true secret
  behind a `VITE_` name.
- Don't log or echo `.env` contents.

## Generated / do-not-edit files

- `src/integrations/supabase/client.ts` and `types.ts` (regenerated by Lovable/Supabase).
- `src/components/ui/*` (shadcn-generated).
- The `public/` folder currently mirrors source files — **`src/` is the source of truth**;
  don't edit the `public/` copies.

## PR / review expectations

- Keep PRs focused; describe what changed and why.
- Ensure `npm run lint`, `npm run test`, and `npm run build` pass before requesting review.
- Don't reformat or churn unrelated files (Lovable round-trips the repo).
- Open PRs as drafts unless told otherwise.

## File routing — where to look first

- **Edit page copy / sections** → `src/components/<Section>.tsx`, wired in
  `src/pages/Index.tsx`.
- **Add a route/page** → `src/pages/`, register in `src/App.tsx` (above `*`).
- **Shared UI primitive** → `src/components/ui/`.
- **Data/Supabase** → `src/integrations/supabase/`.
- **Styling tokens / theme** → `tailwind.config.ts`, `src/index.css`.
- **Build/test/lint config** → `vite.config.ts`, `vitest.config.ts`, `eslint.config.js`,
  `tsconfig*.json`.

## Known pitfalls

- New routes must be added **above** the `*` catch-all in `src/App.tsx`.
- The waitlist form in `HeroSection.tsx` posts to a hardcoded third-party (Formspree)
  endpoint — confirm intent before changing it.
- `@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars` is disabled, so lint won't catch dead code.
- Supabase is configured but barely used; don't assume tables/auth exist.

## What to ask before doing

- Adding a new dependency, framework, or backend (Supabase tables/auth/functions).
- Changing or replacing the waitlist form integration.
- Touching `.env`, secrets, or anything under `public/`'s duplicated source.
- Editing generated files (`supabase/*`, `components/ui/*`).
- Anything that changes deploy/Lovable sync behavior.
